# hyaku tunables — sourced by every slot at the start of each round (edit live; no restart).
# Run 13 (2026-10-30, operator directive: "16-32 lanes per round; all using m_zfl, m_mim or
# m_swe for the roles; 10 rounds sequentially on each, until we reach 100 rounds trained"):
# role map in ~/.omp/agent/config.yml (backup config.yml.pre-run13-20261030) — zfl: task, main,
# planner, reviewer, security-reviewer, scout; mim: connector, critic, mutation-tester,
# sentinel, labrat, seance, distiller, simplifier, sonic, scribe; swe: executor, revenger.
# Wave band 16-32 (ufo-wave-policy.json). Campaign budget: 100 lane-rounds (10 lanes x 10).
# Goal/state: .scratch/goal-20261030-hyaku-run13.md. Labels below unchanged (already @m_zfl).
# In-session campaign (phase 2, 2026-10-20): L1 lane subagents and closure judges run as generic
# `task` agents; operator directive 2026-10-25 (12h run): "all subagents run on m_flash" — every
# role in `task.agentModelOverrides` is pinned to @m_flash (backup: ~/.omp/agent/config.yml.pre-flash-20261025).
# Closures are fresh sessions dispatched by the orchestrator — non-author by session. These values
# are labels for prompts/events; the global role map remains the routing authority.
# Run 8 (2026-10-26, operator-chosen; backup ~/.omp/agent/config.yml.pre-run8-20261026):
# task/main/planner @m_opus; reviewer/mutation-tester/security-reviewer @m_zfl; scout @m_sonnet;
# distiller/seance @m_haiku; connector @m_kfc; executor/labrat/scribe/sonic/simplifier/critic/revenger/sentinel @m_flash.
# Run 9 (2026-10-26): the same run-8 map, unchanged (operator: "use the same model delegations we were using as
# before"); rounds 64-128 seats, 256 hard ceiling; 10-round blocks per lane (.scratch/goal-20261026-hyaku-run9.md).
# Run 11 (2026-10-28, operator-chosen): every role @m_flash except scout @m_grok and
# task @m_zfl (m_flash already :high — "m_flash on high effort"). Rounds 64-128 seats,
# 256 hard ceiling; 10-round blocks per lane (.scratch/goal-20261028-hyaku-run11.md).
# Run 12 (2026-10-29, operator-chosen): task/scout @m_zfl; main/executor/simplifier/sonic/
# scribe/distiller @m_flash; labrat/mutation-tester/sentinel @m_mim; planner/critic/seance
# @m_luna (:max alias); reviewer/connector/security-reviewer @m_kfc; revenger @m_swe
# (operator: "use m_swe instead of m_daybreak"). Backup config.yml.pre-run12-20261029.
# Rounds 64-128 seats, 256 hard ceiling; 10-round blocks per lane
# (.scratch/goal-20261029-hyaku-run12.md). m_kfc chain: dead "@m_swe" hop expanded to
# devin/swe-2:max (run-11 finding: aliases inside fallback chains do not resolve).
# Mid-run operator ruling ("use more m_mim instead of m_luna"): planner/critic/seance
# moved @m_luna -> @m_mim (m_luna out of run 12). Backup
# config.yml.pre-mim-for-luna-20261029.
# Mid-run operator rulings (2026-10-29 ~22:45): "use m_sol 6.1 medium instead of the
# other openai models; unless the task is too trivial, then use gpt-6-luna medium" —
# m_sol = openai-codex/gpt-6.1-sol:medium (was devin/swe-2:max), m_luna =
# openai-codex/gpt-6-luna:medium (was :max), all luna:low chain hops replaced with
# gpt-6.1-sol:medium. "devin/swe-2 is always the ultimate fallback for any model" —
# every fallback chain now ends with devin/swe-2:max (m_muse's dead "@m_swe" alias
# hop expanded). Backup config.yml.pre-sol61-20261029.
# Mid-run operator ruling ("use some m_flash and m_mim"): scout @m_zfl -> @m_flash;
# security-reviewer @m_kfc -> @m_mim. Backup config.yml.pre-flash-mim-balance-20261029.
# Mid-run operator ruling ("insert m_luna as executor"): executor @m_flash -> @m_luna
# (gpt-6-luna:medium). Backup config.yml.pre-executor-luna-20261029.
# Mid-run operator ruling ("swap m_kfc for m_sol 6.1 medium"): reviewer + connector
# @m_kfc -> @m_sol (m_kfc off all roles; chain left in place). Backup
# config.yml.pre-kfc-out-sol-in-20261029.
# Mid-run operator ruling ("use m_zfl and m_kfc here"): reviewer/connector
# @m_sol -> @m_kfc (m_sol off all roles; task stays @m_zfl). Backup
# config.yml.pre-zfl-kfc-20261030.
# Same ruling, full split (dead-primary cleanup): m_zfl carries task, scout,
# mutation-tester, sentinel, sonic, scribe, distiller, simplifier; m_kfc carries
# main, executor, planner, labrat, seance, critic, reviewer, connector,
# security-reviewer. revenger stays @m_swe (operator routing).
# Mid-run operator ruling ("use more concurrency"): task.maxConcurrency 400 -> 800;
# dispatcher LOAD_MAX 2.25x -> 3.5x cores (72 -> 112 on this host), live kernel patched;
# SEAT_CEILING stays 96 (run-9 ruling), HOST_JOB_CAP 100 is the omp binary clamp.
# Second operator ruling ("increase concurrency"): LOAD_MAX 3.5x -> 4.5x cores (112 ->
# 144, live kernel patched), SEAT_CEILING 96 -> 98 (2 below the 100-job omp clamp).
L1_MODEL=@m_zfl
JUDGE_MODEL=@m_zfl
# Lane VCS: jj = lanes are jj-colocated at dispatch/closure time and commit through
# scripts/hyaku/jj-lane.sh (operator 2026-10-20: "jj as git manager from now on on shokunin runs").
HYAKU_VCS=jj
TARGET=100
MAX_ATTEMPTS=3
ROUND_MAXTIME=170m
ROUND_TIMEOUT=180m
CLOSURE_MAXTIME=60m
CLOSURE_TIMEOUT=70m
# Disk guard (operator directive 2026-10-25: every long run ended with /tmp at 100 %).
# scripts/hyaku/disk-guard.sh reads these; inline.sh gates `dispatch`, purges at `advance`, the
# watchdog sweeps each iteration, inline-dispatcher.py gates every seat spawn. Seat scratch lives
# under $HYAKU_SCRATCH/<lane>-r<N>/<seat> (lane-addendum §7). Launch the orchestrator session with
# TMPDIR=$HYAKU_SCRATCH/tmp so seat subprocesses that honour TMPDIR land there too (per-project, not global).
HYAKU_SCRATCH=/fast/scratch/hyaku
HYAKU_DISK_ROOTS="/tmp /var/tmp /fast/scratch/hyaku"
SOFT_PCT=70
TARGET_PCT=60
HARD_PCT=90
IDLE_MIN=45
MIN_AGE_MIN=10
# Mid-run operator ruling (2026-10-30, run 13): "more concurrency" — all 10 block lanes cycle concurrently;
# ~6 L1s live at once (was 4-6); seats fill in tranches under the 98-seat ceiling / 100-job host clamp.
# Mid-run operator rulings (2026-10-30, run 13): "also make concurrency 32-48" — wave band 32-48
# (rounds already dispatched at 16-32 keep their snapshot prompt). "add m_kfc as task role and
# m_luna as fallback for the other roles that get limited on concurrency" — task @m_kfc; luna hop
# added to the m_zfl/m_mim/m_swe fallback chains (terminal devin/swe-2:max preserved).
# Backups: config.yml.pre-run13-20261030, config.yml.pre-kfc-luna-20261030.
# Mid-run operator ruling (2026-10-30, run 13, final): "actually, keep the 32 concurrency" —
# wave band 32-32 (one v1 wave of exactly 32 seats per round; supersedes the 32-48 message).
